    "388": {
      "date": "2026-11-23",
      "edition": "Monday 23 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Play-off draw",
          "heading": "Ireland to face ex-defence coach Les Kiss' Wallabies in fifth-place play-off",
          "body": "Third place in the Northern Hemisphere ladder sends Andy Farrell's side to Twickenham for the Nations Championship fifth-place final, and the opponent is a familiar face. Kiss, the former Ireland defence coach and Ulster boss, succeeded Joe Schmidt as Wallabies head coach earlier this year, and his side sealed third in the Southern Hemisphere table by beating Wales 29-26 on Saturday. All six play-off games are there next weekend, with France meeting South Africa — beaten in Dublin — in the final."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to end losing streak",
          "body": "Mayco Vivas sent off as France beat Argentina 45-17. Scotland's Matt Fagerson injured, extent unknown."
