    "390": {
      "date": "2026-11-23",
      "edition": "Monday 23 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Injury worry",
          "heading": "Matt Fagerson injured in 67-5 Japan rout as Scotland turn to Argentina",
          "body": "Scotland's 67-5 win over Japan at Murrayfield on Saturday left a fitness worry before the Nations Championship finale against Argentina at Twickenham. \"Matt Fagerson went through a lot of work and hopefully his injury isn't serious,\" said Gregor Townsend, who also hailed Ollie Leatherbarrow's work on both sides of the ball. Today's press carries no detail on the extent of it. Stand-in captain Stafford McDowall, deputising for Sione Tuipulotu and Rory Darge, said the side kept their foot on the throat in the second half."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat South Africa, who still reach Nations Championship final",
          "body": "Wallabies beat Wales 29-26 to end losing streak. Mayco Vivas sent off as France beat Argentina 45-17."
