    "391": {
      "date": "2026-11-23",
      "edition": "Monday 23 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Rotation call",
          "heading": "Tandy vows Wales rotation for Japan after 26-29 loss and Williams injury",
          "body": "Wales meet Eddie Jones' Japan for ninth place at Twickenham, a fifth meeting in 16 months, and Tandy insisted: \"It doesn’t matter who wears the shirt – we’ve got to perform.\" Scrum-half Tomos Williams went off early in the second half against Australia with a groin injury and will be assessed. Tandy praised low-cap replacements Kane James, Louie Hennessey and Reuben Morgan-Williams, who all got solid minutes off the bench. Japan have conceded 145 points to England and Scotland over the last two weeks."
        },
        {
          "kicker": "Around the world",
          "heading": "Ireland beat South Africa, who still reach Nations Championship final",
