    "460": {
      "date": "2026-11-23",
      "edition": "Monday 23 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Red-card fallout",
          "heading": "Mayco Vivas red card and early injuries sink Pumas 45-17 in Paris",
          "body": "Saturday's 45-17 defeat in Paris began unravelling before kick-off, when Santiago Chocobares withdrew and Justo Piccardo moved to inside centre. Bautista Delguy and Boris Wenger then went off early and never returned. Piccardo's try and Tomás Albornoz's boot still had Argentina 10-7 up before France led 14-10 at the break. Hollie Davidson's yellow for Vivas became red, Julián Montoya was also carded, and France pulled clear with three tries in quick succession. Scotland await in the battle for seventh."
        },
